course: dictionary
lesson: 12989
title: The experimenter
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An experimenter is a person who does experiments. An experiment is a test, where you try something to find out what happens. «The experimenter planted two beans and gave only one of them water.» The experimenter wanted to find out whether water helps beans grow.
explain: A good experimenter changes just one thing at a time and keeps everything else the same. This is called a fair test. «She put one plant in the sun and the other in a dark cupboard, and kept both the same in every other way.» If both plants grow differently, the sun or the dark must be the reason.
explain: Experimenters also write down what they see. Measuring and recording results helps them remember what happened and decide what it means.
explain: Some experimenters are simply curious people who like trying new things to see what happens. In stories, a bold character can be an experimenter too: Alice eats and drinks different things to see how they change her size.
fact: An experimenter is a person who does experiments.
fact: Experimenter comes from experiment, which means a test to find out what happens.
fact: In science, an experimenter plans a fair test, changes one thing, then measures and records the results.
fact: An experimenter can also be someone who likes trying new things just to see what happens.
fact: Experimenters are curious, so they ask questions such as, «What will happen if I do this?»
exercise: «The experimenter planted two beans and watered only one.» What is an experimenter? | *A person who does experiments | A judge at a school sports day | A person who grows plants in a garden | A person who waters the lawn every day
exercise: In a fair test, what should an experimenter keep the same? | The name of the test | Nothing at all, so there are no results | Only the temperature | *Everything except the one thing being changed
exercise: Which word means a person who does experiments? | experiment | experiments | experimental | *experimenter
test: «Mia, the experimenter, mixed vinegar and baking soda to see what would fizz.» What did Mia do? | She sold sweets at the school fair | She cleaned the science lab floor | *She tested things to see what would happen
test: Why is a good experimenter careful to change only one thing? | So the test takes longer | *So the results show what caused the change | So there is less to write down
exam: Which sentence shows someone acting like an experimenter? | Sam tidied his bedroom before tea | Sam sat on the sofa and read a book all afternoon | *Sam tried a new crisp flavour to see if he liked it
